Cfg-split zk-prover under a default-on `prover` feature, so verify_composed builds without it.

Part of the verifier-only build of SASH eb95bfa that the SP1 segment guest runs
(verifiable-inference-ethereum SPEC.md §1.1). Upstream source is Apache-2.0;
this patch modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

zk-prover turned on stwo's and constraint-framework's `prover` and `parallel`
features unconditionally; stwo's `prover` needs `array_chunks`, which Rust 1.90
removed, so the crate could not build for SP1 v6.10.0's succinct-1.96.0. With
default features the build is upstream's, item for item. Without `prover`
(`cargo check -p zk-prover --no-default-features --lib`) it is the verifier
build: the types, relations, `Plan`, `build_components_linked`, `Verdict`,
`verify_composed`, the binding code and what they call in `gkrlink`,
`gkr_key_tile::verify` and `boundary`.

- prover/Cargo.toml: a default-on `prover` feature turns on stwo/prover,
  stwo/parallel, stwo-constraint-framework/prover and /parallel, and the now
  optional rayon and tracing-subscriber; the stwo crates otherwise come in with
  `default-features = false, features = ["std"]`. `cuda = ["prover"]`, and the
  `zk-prover` binary has `required-features = ["prover"]`. Cargo.lock is
  unchanged.
- prover/build.rs returns before embedding ZK_SOURCE_COMMIT/DIRTY (which runs
  `git -C <crate>/..`) when CARGO_FEATURE_PROVER is unset.
- prover/src/lib.rs gates the prover-only modules (cli, chunks, cudagen,
  cudakernels, dev*, device, device_witness, exprprobe, gencudakernels,
  logup_run, plogup, precache, scalars, shaperoot, spans, witread) and the two
  device re-exports; gadgets/*/mod.rs gate their `device` and `run` modules
  and the `Gadget` impls.
- Every other hunk adds `#[cfg(feature = "prover")]` to a prover-side item
  (witness loading and synthesis, trace and interaction builders, every
  `cuda_eval_blob` override, every rayon use, util.rs's host introspection:
  add_phase, mark_timeline, modes_json, nvidia_smi, gpu_name, env_json,
  unsound_skips, provenance_json, emit; gkr_key_tile's cmd, tamper and its
  gkr_prover/mle imports; compose's generate, prove_layer, prove_gen,
  prove_gen_to, Gen, prewarm_blobs, fp_rows, provers), or splits a `use` list
  to attach one. Function bodies on the verify path are unchanged.
- compose.rs, verify_composed: `t0` and the `Verdict.verify_secs` field and
  its two initialisers are prover-only (std has no clock on the zkVM target).
  `shape_root_check`, `shape_root_from_params` and their `catch_unwind` are
  prover-only; without `prover`, verify_composed binds
  `(None, None, 0.0, None)`, what upstream's shape_root_check returns when no
  calibration is set. Placing the attribute on the two struct-literal fields
  moves each `verify_secs:` initialiser onto its own line.

